{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183276468,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fb36eeffe9w9O3m4PshLj5X","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_BTnQHANaCN5xLMgGuLKgmD61","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python -c \"import json, pathlib; p=pathlib.Path('/workspace/out/module_map.json'); data=json.loads(p.read_text()); required=['modules','entry_points','dependency_edges','key_functions','runtime_flows']; missing=[k for k in required if k not in data]; assert not missing, missing; assert any(ep.get('identifier')=='minisvc.cli:main' for ep in data['entry_points']); assert any(ep.get('identifier')=='minisvc.api.routes:register_routes' for ep in data['entry_points']); print('module_map.json ok')\"","workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"/usr/bin/bash: line 1: python: command not found\n","metadata":{"output":"/usr/bin/bash: line 1: python: command not found\n","exit":127,"truncated":false},"title":"python -c \"import json, pathlib; p=pathlib.Path('/workspace/out/module_map.json'); data=json.loads(p.read_text()); required=['modules','entry_points','dependency_edges','key_functions','runtime_flows']; missing=[k for k in required if k not in data]; assert not missing, missing; assert any(ep.get('identifier')=='minisvc.cli:main' for ep in data['entry_points']); assert any(ep.get('identifier')=='minisvc.api.routes:register_routes' for ep in data['entry_points']); print('module_map.json ok')\"","time":{"start":1788183276466,"end":1788183276467}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b53572aed56503c016a9582ec396487d295d423784968e851"}},"id":"prt_058076ba4001xpH5OqGnEwaFIq","sessionID":"ses_fa7fb36eeffe9w9O3m4PshLj5X","messageID":"msg_0580751850011QaFuyPLMCD9bH"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183276514,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fb36eeffe9w9O3m4PshLj5X","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_42YkUnysPWQPlyMKk12kyk2d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out/architecture.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out/architecture.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # minisvc Architecture Summary\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: \n5: `minisvc` is a small Python service skeleton centered on one domain object: `Order`. The codebase contains a CLI bootstrap path, route registration helpers for an HTTP adapter, simple request handlers, and a SQLite-backed repository.\n6: \n7: The active runtime code is concentrated in:\n8: \n9: - `minisvc/cli.py`\n10: - `minisvc/config.py`\n11: - `minisvc/models.py`\n12: - `minisvc/api/routes.py`\n13: - `minisvc/api/handlers.py`\n14: - `minisvc/audit.py`\n15: - `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n16: \n17: The package marker files `minisvc/__init__.py`, `minisvc/api/__init__.py`, and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are not business-logic modules.\n18: \n19: ## Modules\n20: \n21: | Module | Purpose |\n22: | --- | --- |\n23: | `minisvc.cli` | CLI bootstrap. Loads settings, creates `OrderRepository`, initializes schema, and prints readiness. |\n24: | `minisvc.config` | Defines frozen `Settings` and loads `MINISVC_DB` plus `MINISVC_READONLY` from the environment. |\n25: | `minisvc.models` | Defines the `Order` dataclass shared across layers. |\n26: | `minisvc.api.routes` | Registers HTTP routes by mapping framework callbacks to handler functions. |\n27: | `minisvc.api.handlers` | Converts payloads into `Order` instances, calls the repository, and shapes HTTP responses. |\n28: | `minisvc.audit` | Builds order event dictionaries for responses. No persistence. |\n29: | `minisvc.storage.repo` | Encapsulates SQLite schema creation, inserts, and reads for orders. |\n30: \n31: ## Entry Points\n32: \n33: - `minisvc.cli:main`\n34:   `pyproject.toml` exposes this as the `minisvc` console script.\n35: - `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`\n36:   This is the HTTP integration point. A caller must pass an app object with `post` and `get` registration methods plus a repository instance.\n37: \n38: ## Data Flow\n39: \n40: ### CLI startup flow\n41: \n42: 1. The console script resolves to `minisvc.cli:main`.\n43: 2. `main` loads settings from `os.environ` via `load_settings`.\n44: 3. `main` instantiates `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)`.\n45: 4. `main` calls `repo.init_schema()` to ensure the `orders` table exists.\n46: 5. `main` prints a ready message and exits.\n47: \n48: This path prepares storage but does not run an HTTP server.\n49: \n50: ### HTTP create-order flow\n51: \n52: 1. Some outer application calls `register_routes(app, repo)`.\n53: 2. `register_routes` binds POST `/orders` to `create_order(payload, repo)`.\n54: 3. `create_order` reads `order_id`, `customer`, and `total_cents` directly from the request payload.\n55: 4. It constructs an `Order` dataclass and calls `repo.save(order)`.\n56: 5. `repo.save` opens a SQLite connection and inserts into the `orders` table.\n57: 6. `create_order` builds an event dict with `order_event(order, \"created\")`.\n58: 7. The handler returns `{\"status\": \"created\", \"order_id\": ..., \"event\": ...}`.\n59: \n60: ### HTTP read-order flow\n61: \n62: 1. `register_routes` binds GET `/orders/<order_id>` to `get_order(order_id, repo)`.\n63: 2. `get_order` calls `repo.get(order_id)`.\n64: 3. `repo.get` queries SQLite and either returns `Order(...)` or `None`.\n65: 4. The handler returns either a `missing` response or an `ok` response with `order.__dict__` and a computed read event.\n66: \n67: ## Storage\n68: \n69: - Storage backend: local SQLite database via `sqlite3`.\n70: - Configured by: `MINISVC_DB`, defaulting to `orders.sqlite`.\n71: - Schema owner: `OrderRepository.init_schema()`.\n72: - Tables created by code: `orders` only.\n73: \n74: Important limitation: there is no audit table, no migration layer, and no explicit durability tuning beyond SQLite's defaults.\n75: \n76: ## Risks And Extension Points\n77: \n78: ### Risks\n79: \n80: - `MINISVC_READONLY` is parsed but never enforced. Write paths still call `repo.save`.\n81: - `create_order` has no retry behavior despite the README design note.\n82: - Audit behavior is response-only. `order_event` returns a dict and does not persist anything.\n83: - Request validation is thin. Missing fields, bad integer conversion, or duplicate keys will raise exceptions.\n84: - The CLI initializes schema, but the HTTP path shown here has no guaranteed bootstrap step unless the embedding app calls it.\n85: \n86: ### Extension points\n87: \n88: - Add a service layer between handlers and storage if business rules grow.\n89: - Replace route lambdas with explicit adapter functions if framework-specific request/response handling is needed.\n90: - Introduce durable audit persistence in `storage` or a separate repository.\n91: - Enforce readonly behavior either in handlers, a service layer, or the repository.\n92: - Add structured validation around `create_order` inputs before constructing `Order`.\n\n(End of file - total 92 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# minisvc Architecture Summary\n\n## Overview\n\n`minisvc` is a small Python service skeleton centered on one domain object: `Order`. The codebase contains a CLI bootstrap path, route registration helpers for an HTTP adapter, simple request handlers, and a SQLite-backed repository.\n\nThe active runtime code is concentrated in:\n\n- `minisvc/cli.py`\n- `minisvc/config.py`\n- `minisvc/models.py`\n- `minisvc/api/routes.py`\n- `minisvc/api/handlers.py`\n- `minisvc/audit.py`\n- `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n\nThe package marker files `minisvc/__init__.py`, `minisvc/api/__init__.py`, and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are not business-logic modules.\n\n## Modules\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/out/architecture.md","text":"# minisvc Architecture Summary\n\n## Overview\n\n`minisvc` is a small Python service skeleton centered on one domain object: `Order`. The codebase contains a CLI bootstrap path, route registration helpers for an HTTP adapter, simple request handlers, and a SQLite-backed repository.\n\nThe active runtime code is concentrated in:\n\n- `minisvc/cli.py`\n- `minisvc/config.py`\n- `minisvc/models.py`\n- `minisvc/api/routes.py`\n- `minisvc/api/handlers.py`\n- `minisvc/audit.py`\n- `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n\nThe package marker files `minisvc/__init__.py`, `minisvc/api/__init__.py`, and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are not business-logic modules.\n\n## Modules\n\n| Module | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `minisvc.cli` | CLI bootstrap. Loads settings, creates `OrderRepository`, initializes schema, and prints readiness. |\n| `minisvc.config` | Defines frozen `Settings` and loads `MINISVC_DB` plus `MINISVC_READONLY` from the environment. |\n| `minisvc.models` | Defines the `Order` dataclass shared across layers. |\n| `minisvc.api.routes` | Registers HTTP routes by mapping framework callbacks to handler functions. |\n| `minisvc.api.handlers` | Converts payloads into `Order` instances, calls the repository, and shapes HTTP responses. |\n| `minisvc.audit` | Builds order event dictionaries for responses. No persistence. |\n| `minisvc.storage.repo` | Encapsulates SQLite schema creation, inserts, and reads for orders. |\n\n## Entry Points\n\n- `minisvc.cli:main`\n  `pyproject.toml` exposes this as the `minisvc` console script.\n- `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`\n  This is the HTTP integration point. A caller must pass an app object with `post` and `get` registration methods plus a repository instance.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n### CLI startup flow\n\n1. The console script resolves to `minisvc.cli:main`.\n2. `main` loads settings from `os.environ` via `load_settings`.\n3. `main` instantiates `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)`.\n4. `main` calls `repo.init_schema()` to ensure the `orders` table exists.\n5. `main` prints a ready message and exits.\n\nThis path prepares storage but does not run an HTTP server.\n\n### HTTP create-order flow\n\n1. Some outer application calls `register_routes(app, repo)`.\n2. `register_routes` binds POST `/orders` to `create_order(payload, repo)`.\n3. `create_order` reads `order_id`, `customer`, and `total_cents` directly from the request payload.\n4. It constructs an `Order` dataclass and calls `repo.save(order)`.\n5. `repo.save` opens a SQLite connection and inserts into the `orders` table.\n6. `create_order` builds an event dict with `order_event(order, \"created\")`.\n7. The handler returns `{\"status\": \"created\", \"order_id\": ..., \"event\": ...}`.\n\n### HTTP read-order flow\n\n1. `register_routes` binds GET `/orders/<order_id>` to `get_order(order_id, repo)`.\n2. `get_order` calls `repo.get(order_id)`.\n3. `repo.get` queries SQLite and either returns `Order(...)` or `None`.\n4. The handler returns either a `missing` response or an `ok` response with `order.__dict__` and a computed read event.\n\n## Storage\n\n- Storage backend: local SQLite database via `sqlite3`.\n- Configured by: `MINISVC_DB`, defaulting to `orders.sqlite`.\n- Schema owner: `OrderRepository.init_schema()`.\n- Tables created by code: `orders` only.\n\nImportant limitation: there is no audit table, no migration layer, and no explicit durability tuning beyond SQLite's defaults.\n\n## Risks And Extension Points\n\n### Risks\n\n- `MINISVC_READONLY` is parsed but never enforced. Write paths still call `repo.save`.\n- `create_order` has no retry behavior despite the README design note.\n- Audit behavior is response-only. `order_event` returns a dict and does not persist anything.\n- Request validation is thin. Missing fields, bad integer conversion, or duplicate keys will raise exceptions.\n- The CLI initializes schema, but the HTTP path shown here has no guaranteed bootstrap step unless the embedding app calls it.\n\n### Extension points\n\n- Add a service layer between handlers and storage if business rules grow.\n- Replace route lambdas with explicit adapter functions if framework-specific request/response handling is needed.\n- Introduce durable audit persistence in `storage` or a separate repository.\n- Enforce readonly behavior either in handlers, a service layer, or the repository.\n- Add structured validation around `create_order` inputs before constructing `Order`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":92,"totalLines":92,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out/architecture.md","time":{"start":1788183276506,"end":1788183276514}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b53572aed56503c016a9582ec397887d2af1dd8ec664e9b31"}},"id":"prt_058076bb8001OqxOleD7HnlZ3o","sessionID":"ses_fa7fb36eeffe9w9O3m4PshLj5X","messageID":"msg_0580751850011QaFuyPLMCD9bH"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183276561,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fb36eeffe9w9O3m4PshLj5X","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_prvzUHSBBGnM7Azh2QaX7ENX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n2: \"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-13 loads readonly into Settings, but minisvc/cli.py:7-12 and minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 never check settings.readonly before calling minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 save()\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may believe production is protected from writes when it is not.\"\n3: \"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) exactly once and does not catch exceptions; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 has no retry loop\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient SQLite failures surface immediately and behavior differs from operational expectations.\"\n4: \"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns an in-memory dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-30 creates and uses only the orders table\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may assume compliance or traceability guarantees that the implementation does not provide.\"\n5: \"The fixture has an HTTP adapter and CLI bootstrap command\",\"README.md:3\",\"pyproject.toml:6-7 defines minisvc.cli:main; minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 exposes register_routes(app, repo) for HTTP route registration\",\"confirmed\",\"Low risk; this summary matches the implemented structure.\"\n\n(End of file - total 5 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-13 loads readonly into Settings, but minisvc/cli.py:7-12 and minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 never check settings.readonly before calling minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 save()\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may believe production is protected from writes when it is not.\"\n\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) exactly once and does not catch exceptions; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 has no retry loop\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient SQLite failures surface immediately and behavior differs from operational expectations.\"\n\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns an in-memory dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-30 creates and uses only the orders table\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may assume compliance or traceability guarantees that the implementation does not provide.\"\n\"The fixture has an HTTP adapter and CLI bootstrap command\",\"README.md:3\",\"pyproject.toml:6-7 defines minisvc.cli:main; minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 exposes register_routes(app, repo) for HTTP route registration\",\"confirmed\",\"Low risk; this summary matches the implemented structure.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv","text":"claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-13 loads readonly into Settings, but minisvc/cli.py:7-12 and minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 never check settings.readonly before calling minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 save()\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may believe production is protected from writes when it is not.\"\n\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) exactly once and does not catch exceptions; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 has no retry loop\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient SQLite failures surface immediately and behavior differs from operational expectations.\"\n\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns an in-memory dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-30 creates and uses only the orders table\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may assume compliance or traceability guarantees that the implementation does not provide.\"\n\"The fixture has an HTTP adapter and CLI bootstrap command\",\"README.md:3\",\"pyproject.toml:6-7 defines minisvc.cli:main; minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 exposes register_routes(app, repo) for HTTP route registration\",\"confirmed\",\"Low risk; this summary matches the implemented structure.\"","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":5,"totalLines":5,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv","time":{"start":1788183276553,"end":1788183276560}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b53572aed56503c016a9582ec398487d2b1a826d10fefa903"}},"id":"prt_058076bf5001UchDDzc3QV3p4H","sessionID":"ses_fa7fb36eeffe9w9O3m4PshLj5X","messageID":"msg_0580751850011QaFuyPLMCD9bH"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183276616,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fb36eeffe9w9O3m4PshLj5X","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Vi7AWUoKJewef5uY0B7kZKRN","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out/risk_register.csv</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\n2: R1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-30 uses a local SQLite file with one-table schema creation and direct inserts; no migration/versioning or backup hooks are present\",\"Schema drift, local file corruption, or deployment-specific filesystem behavior can cause data loss or failed startups\",\"Add schema migration/versioning, document filesystem expectations, and add backup or export procedures\",\"Backend owner\"\n3: R2,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 returns a dict only; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-30 creates no audit table\",\"No durable audit trail exists for create or read operations despite documentation implying one\",\"Persist audit events through a repository/table or emit them to an external durable sink\",\"Backend owner or compliance-focused engineer\"\n4: R3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-13 parses MINISVC_READONLY, but minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 and minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 never enforce it\",\"Runtime safety flags can be assumed active while writes still occur\",\"Thread readonly configuration into the request path or repository and reject writes when enabled\",\"Service owner\"\n5: R4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 indexes payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(...); no validation or exception handling is present\",\"Malformed requests can raise uncaught exceptions or create inconsistent API behavior\",\"Validate payload shape and types before model construction and convert failures into explicit client errors\",\"API owner\"\n6: R5,HTTP bootstrap coupling,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes caller-provided app and repo; minisvc/cli.py:7-12 initializes schema separately and does not assemble the HTTP runtime\",\"An embedding app can register routes without initializing schema or consistent config\",\"Provide a single application factory that loads config, initializes storage, and registers routes together\",\"Platform or integration owner\"\n7: R6,error handling/retry,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:12 calls repo.save(order) once; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 exposes sqlite errors directly\",\"Transient database errors and duplicate key failures bubble up without controlled responses or retries\",\"Define error mapping and retry policy at handler or service boundary\",\"Backend owner\"\n\n(End of file - total 7 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-30 uses a local SQLite file with one-table schema creation and direct inserts; no migration/versioning or backup hooks are present\",\"Schema drift, local file corruption, or deployment-specific filesystem behavior can cause data loss or failed startups\",\"Add schema migration/versioning, document filesystem expectations, and add backup or export procedures\",\"Backend owner\"\nR2,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 returns a dict only; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-30 creates no audit table\",\"No durable audit trail exists for create or read operations despite documentation implying one\",\"Persist audit events through a repository/table or emit them to an external durable sink\",\"Backend owner or compliance-focused engineer\"\nR3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-13 parses MINISVC_READONLY, but minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 and minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 never enforce it\",\"Runtime safety flags can be assumed active while writes still occur\",\"Thread readonly configuration into the request path or repository and reject writes when enabled\",\"Service owner\"\nR4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 indexes payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(...); no validation or exception handling is present\",\"Malformed requests can raise uncaught exceptions or create inconsistent API behavior\",\"Validate payload shape and types before model construction and convert failures into explicit client errors\",\"API owner\"\nR5,HTTP bootstrap coupling,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes caller-provided app and repo; minisvc/cli.py:7-12 initializes schema separately and does not assemble the HTTP runtime\",\"An embedding app can register routes without initializing schema or consistent config\",\"Provide a single application factory that loads config, initializes storage, and registers routes together\",\"Platform or integration owner\"\nR6,error handling/retry,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:12 calls repo.save(order) once; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 exposes sqlite errors directly\",\"Transient database errors and duplicate key failures bubble up without controlled responses or retries\",\"Define error mapping and retry policy at handler or service boundary\",\"Backend owner\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv","text":"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-30 uses a local SQLite file with one-table schema creation and direct inserts; no migration/versioning or backup hooks are present\",\"Schema drift, local file corruption, or deployment-specific filesystem behavior can cause data loss or failed startups\",\"Add schema migration/versioning, document filesystem expectations, and add backup or export procedures\",\"Backend owner\"\nR2,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 returns a dict only; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-30 creates no audit table\",\"No durable audit trail exists for create or read operations despite documentation implying one\",\"Persist audit events through a repository/table or emit them to an external durable sink\",\"Backend owner or compliance-focused engineer\"\nR3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-13 parses MINISVC_READONLY, but minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 and minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 never enforce it\",\"Runtime safety flags can be assumed active while writes still occur\",\"Thread readonly configuration into the request path or repository and reject writes when enabled\",\"Service owner\"\nR4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 indexes payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(...); no validation or exception handling is present\",\"Malformed requests can raise uncaught exceptions or create inconsistent API behavior\",\"Validate payload shape and types before model construction and convert failures into explicit client errors\",\"API owner\"\nR5,HTTP bootstrap coupling,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes caller-provided app and repo; minisvc/cli.py:7-12 initializes schema separately and does not assemble the HTTP runtime\",\"An embedding app can register routes without initializing schema or consistent config\",\"Provide a single application factory that loads config, initializes storage, and registers routes together\",\"Platform or integration owner\"\nR6,error handling/retry,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:12 calls repo.save(order) once; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 exposes sqlite errors directly\",\"Transient database errors and duplicate key failures bubble up without controlled responses or retries\",\"Define error mapping and retry policy at handler or service boundary\",\"Backend owner\"","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":7,"totalLines":7,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out/risk_register.csv","time":{"start":1788183276610,"end":1788183276615}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b53572aed56503c016a9582ec399087d2b1bdc8ef0fe3ed06"}},"id":"prt_058076c1f001k2nGnrNqWmHUwg","sessionID":"ses_fa7fb36eeffe9w9O3m4PshLj5X","messageID":"msg_0580751850011QaFuyPLMCD9bH"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183276698,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fb36eeffe9w9O3m4PshLj5X","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_nHOj5dqwN4iS7ov9MmRtuZgn","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # New Engineer Onboarding Plan\n2: \n3: ## What Is Runtime Code\n4: \n5: Read and reason about these first because they drive actual behavior:\n6: \n7: 1. `minisvc/cli.py`\n8: 2. `minisvc/config.py`\n9: 3. `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n10: 4. `minisvc/api/handlers.py`\n11: 5. `minisvc/api/routes.py`\n12: 6. `minisvc/audit.py`\n13: 7. `minisvc/models.py`\n14: \n15: Treat these as non-business-logic files:\n16: \n17: - `minisvc/__init__.py`\n18: - `minisvc/api/__init__.py`\n19: - `minisvc/storage/__init__.py`\n20: \n21: ## Recommended Read Order\n22: \n23: 1. `README.md`\n24: 2. `pyproject.toml`\n25: 3. `minisvc/models.py`\n26: 4. `minisvc/config.py`\n27: 5. `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n28: 6. `minisvc/api/handlers.py`\n29: 7. `minisvc/api/routes.py`\n30: 8. `minisvc/cli.py`\n31: 9. `minisvc/audit.py`\n32: \n33: This order moves from top-level intent to domain model, then storage, then request handling and bootstrapping.\n34: \n35: ## Local Run And Test Commands\n36: \n37: Run from the repo root.\n38: \n39: ```bash\n40: python -m pip install -e .\n41: minisvc\n42: ```\n43: \n44: Useful variations:\n45: \n46: ```bash\n47: MINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc-orders.sqlite minisvc\n48: python -m compileall minisvc\n49: ```\n50: \n51: There are no automated tests in the fixture repository, so `compileall` is only a syntax smoke check.\n52: \n53: ## First Debugging Breakpoint Or Trace Point\n54: \n55: Start with `minisvc/api/handlers.py` inside `create_order` just before `repo.save(order)`.\n56: \n57: Why this point:\n58: \n59: - It shows the raw payload-to-model conversion.\n60: - It is where validation problems and integer conversion issues surface.\n61: - It leads directly into the persistence boundary in `OrderRepository.save`.\n62: \n63: If you are tracing startup instead, begin at `minisvc/cli.py:main` and step into `load_settings` and `repo.init_schema()`.\n64: \n65: ## Two Safe First Changes\n66: \n67: 1. Add explicit request validation and friendly error responses around missing keys and bad `total_cents` values in `minisvc/api/handlers.py`.\n68: 2. Enforce `MINISVC_READONLY` on the write path, either before `repo.save(order)` or inside `OrderRepository.save`.\n69: \n70: Both changes are small, localized, and aligned with documented expectations.\n\n(End of file - total 70 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# New Engineer Onboarding Plan\n\n## What Is Runtime Code\n\nRead and reason about these first because they drive actual behavior:\n\n1. `minisvc/cli.py`\n2. `minisvc/config.py`\n3. `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n4. `minisvc/api/handlers.py`\n5. `minisvc/api/routes.py`\n6. `minisvc/audit.py`\n7. `minisvc/models.py`\n\nTreat these as non-business-logic files:\n\n- `minisvc/__init__.py`\n- `minisvc/api/__init__.py`\n- `minisvc/storage/__init__.py`\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","text":"# New Engineer Onboarding Plan\n\n## What Is Runtime Code\n\nRead and reason about these first because they drive actual behavior:\n\n1. `minisvc/cli.py`\n2. `minisvc/config.py`\n3. `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n4. `minisvc/api/handlers.py`\n5. `minisvc/api/routes.py`\n6. `minisvc/audit.py`\n7. `minisvc/models.py`\n\nTreat these as non-business-logic files:\n\n- `minisvc/__init__.py`\n- `minisvc/api/__init__.py`\n- `minisvc/storage/__init__.py`\n\n## Recommended Read Order\n\n1. `README.md`\n2. `pyproject.toml`\n3. `minisvc/models.py`\n4. `minisvc/config.py`\n5. `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n6. `minisvc/api/handlers.py`\n7. `minisvc/api/routes.py`\n8. `minisvc/cli.py`\n9. `minisvc/audit.py`\n\nThis order moves from top-level intent to domain model, then storage, then request handling and bootstrapping.\n\n## Local Run And Test Commands\n\nRun from the repo root.\n\n```bash\npython -m pip install -e .\nminisvc\n```\n\nUseful variations:\n\n```bash\nMINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc-orders.sqlite minisvc\npython -m compileall minisvc\n```\n\nThere are no automated tests in the fixture repository, so `compileall` is only a syntax smoke check.\n\n## First Debugging Breakpoint Or Trace Point\n\nStart with `minisvc/api/handlers.py` inside `create_order` just before `repo.save(order)`.\n\nWhy this point:\n\n- It shows the raw payload-to-model conversion.\n- It is where validation problems and integer conversion issues surface.\n- It leads directly into the persistence boundary in `OrderRepository.save`.\n\nIf you are tracing startup instead, begin at `minisvc/cli.py:main` and step into `load_settings` and `repo.init_schema()`.\n\n## Two Safe First Changes\n\n1. Add explicit request validation and friendly error responses around missing keys and bad `total_cents` values in `minisvc/api/handlers.py`.\n2. Enforce `MINISVC_READONLY` on the write path, either before `repo.save(order)` or inside `OrderRepository.save`.\n\nBoth changes are small, localized, and aligned with documented expectations.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":70,"totalLines":70,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","time":{"start":1788183276688,"end":1788183276697}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b53572aed56503c016a9582ec399887d2b211b26b016284c4"}},"id":"prt_058076c53001uL4COr0hBLqyDf","sessionID":"ses_fa7fb36eeffe9w9O3m4PshLj5X","messageID":"msg_0580751850011QaFuyPLMCD9bH"}}
